<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <div class="space-y-8 max-w-4xl">
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">How Wiretap works</h1>
      <p class="opacity-80">
        The harness is an ordinary Phoenix app that never knows it is being observed.
        Wiretap attaches from outside — read-only toward the host — and every panel in the
        <a href="/demo" class="link">ATC console</a>
        maps to a public library call.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded border p-4 space-y-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">The flow</h2>
      <pre class="font-mono text-xs leading-snug overflow-x-auto" phx-no-curly-interpolation>
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ HARNESS — unmodified host app                                          │
│                                                                        │
│   Harness.Tower ────── broadcast ─────▶ Phoenix.PubSub                 │
│   flights enter, transmit               (Harness.PubSub)               │
│   positions every 2s, land              "flight:WT-101", "atc:events"  │
│                                                │                       │
│                                                ▼                       │
│                                     Registry (duplicate-key ETS)       │
│                                     topic ──▶ [subscriber pids]        │
│                                                ▲                       │
│   HarnessWeb.DemoLive ── subscribe/unsubscribe ┘                       │
│     track a flight   = subscribe("flight:WT-101")                      │
│     hand off         = unsubscribe (clean path)                        │
│     walk off shift   = no unsubscribe — the LEAK                       │
└──────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │  Registry.select/2 — reads only,
                               │  from outside, zero host changes
                               ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ WIRETAP — the library under demonstration                              │
│                                                                        │
│   Wiretap.Snapshot ── take/1 ──▶ topic → [pids]   (layer 1)            │
│         │                                                              │
│   session without :trace         │  session with trace: true           │
│         ▼                        │        ▼                            │
│   Wiretap.Snapshotter            │  Wiretap.Tracer  (layer 2)          │
│     polls + diffs per interval   │    OTP trace session on             │
│     :joined/:left ≈ approximate  │    subscribe/unsubscribe:           │
│     monitors → left_by_death     │    exact events, {:caller}          │
│         │                        │    attribution, VM-level topic      │
│         │                        │    prefix filters, monitors →       │
│         │                        │    left_by_death                    │
│         │                        │        │                            │
│         └───────────┬────────────┴────────┘                            │
│                     ▼                                                  │
│   Wiretap.Collector ── per-session ETS ring buffer (10k events)        │
│         ▲                    heir: SessionManager, so events           │
│         │                    outlive the session                       │
│   Wiretap.SessionManager ── budgets (events / duration / rate),        │
│                             teardown on stop/expiry/crash,             │
│                             telemetry ([:wiretap, ...])                │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
      </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded border p-4 space-y-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Every demo surface is a public library call</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="table table-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Where you see it</th>
              <th>What it calls</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="font-mono text-sm">
            <tr>
              <td>Registry truth panel</td>
              <td>Wiretap.snapshot(Harness.PubSub)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Wiretap sessions card</td>
              <td>Wiretap.watch/2 · stop/1 · sessions/0 · events/1</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Roll Call dashboard page</td>
              <td>Wiretap.Snapshot.roll_call/1 (via Wiretap.DashboardPage)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Harness LiveView tests</td>
              <td>Wiretap.Test.assert_subscribed/refute_subscribed</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Tower telemetry on a Timeline (the v0.2 bridge; tower emits entered/landed/transmission)
              </td>
              <td>Wiretap.watch(pubsub, telemetry: [[:harness, :tower, :entered]])</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Your own traffic from iex (manual radio; burst to trip budgets on purpose)</td>
              <td>Harness.Transmit.broadcast/2 · to_flight/2 · atc/1 · burst/3</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Standalone UI (:4008) Roll Call + Timeline + Sessions + Docs</td>
              <td>Wiretap.Snapshot.roll_call/2 · Wiretap.events/1 · sessions/0 · watch/2 trace: true</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Row inspectors (transmissions here; Timeline rows + Roll Call topics in the Wiretap UI)</td>
              <td>Wiretap.events/1 by seq · Wiretap.subscribers/2 — each modal shows its headless twin</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Sessions card "exact (call tracing)" toggle</td>
              <td>Wiretap.watch(Harness.PubSub, trace: true)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm opacity-70">
        The demo's own PubSub traffic deliberately uses plain Phoenix.PubSub — Wiretap's
        contract is that the host is never modified and pays nothing while the tool is idle.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded border p-4 space-y-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Sessions, budgets, and the event pipeline</h2>
      <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
        A capture session polls the registry on an interval, diffs consecutive snapshots,
        and records events. Every session carries three budgets — max events, max
        duration, and max rate (events/sec) — and hitting any bound expires it
        automatically. Every event carries two axes: <span class="font-mono">kind</span>
        (what happened: joined, left) and <span class="font-mono">source</span>
        (how Wiretap knows: snapshot polling is approximate; sessions armed with
        <span class="font-mono">trace: true</span>
        record exact, caller-attributed
        events through OTP trace sessions — no polling gap).
      </p>
      <pre class="font-mono text-xs leading-snug overflow-x-auto" phx-no-curly-interpolation>
   Wiretap.watch/2                     stop/1        budget hit      crash
        │                                 │               │            │
        ▼                                 ▼               ▼            ▼
    [running] ──────────────────────▶ [stopped]      [expired]    [crashed]
        │                                 └───────────────┴────────────┘
        │ records :joined / :left                 events remain readable
        ▼                                         (ring buffer outlives
    Wiretap.events(session)                        the session)
      </pre>
      <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
        Wiretap also emits telemetry about itself:
        <span class="font-mono">[:wiretap, :session, :start | :stop]</span>
        (span convention), <span class="font-mono">[:wiretap, :budget, :exhausted]</span>
        (the alarm to page on), <span class="font-mono">[:wiretap, :collector, :dropped]</span>
        (receiver overload — watermark drops),
        and <span class="font-mono">[:wiretap, :registry, :incompatible]</span>
        (shape-probe
        failure — the library refuses to report wrong data). To watch them from the
        console while driving the demo: <span class="font-mono">Harness.TelemetryDebug.on()</span>
        — the <span class="font-mono">.iex.exs</span>
        banner has the one-liners.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded border p-4 space-y-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Reproduce a subscription leak in 60 seconds</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-sm space-y-1 opacity-90">
        <li>Open the <a href="/demo" class="link">ATC console</a> and start a wiretap session</li>
        <li>Click two flights in the Airspace column — registry truth shows both topics</li>
        <li>
          Click "walk off shift (leaky)" — your scope reads empty, the leak counter ticks up
        </li>
        <li>Registry truth still lists both flight topics: those are the leaks</li>
        <li>Leaked reports keep arriving in the transmissions feed, badged "leaked" —
          click one and the modal shows "tracked at receipt: no — leaked delivery"</li>
        <li>Open <a href="/dashboard/wiretap" class="link">Roll Call</a>: the leaked topics list
          your LiveView pid as a subscriber</li>
        <li>Check the session's captured events — the :joined edges have no matching :left</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded border p-4 space-y-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Headless, from iex</h2>
      <pre class="font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto" phx-no-curly-interpolation><code>iex -S mix phx.server

Wiretap.snapshot(Harness.PubSub)          # topic → subscriber pids, right now
Wiretap.topics(Harness.PubSub)
Wiretap.subscribers(Harness.PubSub, "atc:events")

{:ok, s} = Wiretap.watch(Harness.PubSub, interval_ms: 250)
Wiretap.events(s)                         # joined/left events with pid labels

{:ok, b} = Wiretap.watch(Harness.PubSub, telemetry: [[:harness, :tower, :entered]])
Wiretap.events(b)                         # host telemetry on the timeline (v0.2 bridge)

Harness.Transmit.broadcast("station:alpha", {:msg, "hello"})  # your own traffic
Harness.Transmit.burst("atc:events", 500) # trip a max_rate budget on purpose

{:ok, t} = Wiretap.watch(Harness.PubSub, trace: [prefixes: ["flight:"]])
Wiretap.events(t)                         # exact events with caller attribution
Wiretap.sessions()                        # budgets and status
Wiretap.stop(s)</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
